        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Simplify <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Simplify [MATH: \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We subtract the exponents, as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (x^{2})/(x^{3})|=; x^{(2 \u2212 3)}|=; x^{\u2212 1}]</span></p><p>Then, we convert the negative exponent to a positive exponent by taking the reciprocal:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^{\u2212 1}|= (1)/(x)]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3} = \\dfrac 1 x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We subtract the exponents, as follows:\n\n[MATH: (x^{2})/(x^{3})|=; x^{(2 \u2212 3)}|=; x^{\u2212 1}]\n\nThen, we convert the negative exponent to a positive exponent by taking the reciprocal:\n\n[MATH: x^{\u2212 1}|= (1)/(x)]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3} = \\dfrac 1 x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSimplify [MATH: \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe subtract the exponents, as follows:\n\n[MATH: (x^{2})/(x^{3})|=; x^{(2 \u2212 3)}|=; x^{\u2212 1}]\n\nThen, we convert the negative exponent to a positive exponent by taking the reciprocal:\n\n[MATH: x^{\u2212 1}|= (1)/(x)]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3} = \\dfrac 1 x.]"
      },
