          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (p^{7})/(p^{2}) \u22c5 p^{3}|=; p^{(7 \u2212 2)} \u22c5 p^{3}|=; p^{5} \u22c5 p^{3}]</span></p><p>Then we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: p^{5} \u22c5 p^{3}|=; p^{(5 + 3)}|=; p^{8}]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (p^{7})/(p^{2}) \u22c5 p^{3} = p^{8}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n[MATH: (p^{7})/(p^{2}) \u22c5 p^{3}|=; p^{(7 \u2212 2)} \u22c5 p^{3}|=; p^{5} \u22c5 p^{3}]\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n[MATH: p^{5} \u22c5 p^{3}|=; p^{(5 + 3)}|=; p^{8}]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: (p^{7})/(p^{2}) \u22c5 p^{3} = p^{8}.]",
